WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Sometimes the answer is in a file.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.215
This video shows how a person attaches a document to a chat, how

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:11.622
the assistant answers from it, and how it can read the charts inside it.

00:00:11.622 --> 00:00:14.390
It also shows the settings that control it.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.504
A person has a file and a question:

00:00:21.504 --> 00:00:23.772
a policy, a report, a contract.

00:00:23.772 --> 00:00:28.370
They should not wait for an administrator to add it to the assistant.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.098
With attachments on, the person attaches the file to the chat and asks.

00:00:34.098 --> 00:00:37.330
The assistant reads it, and answers from it.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.444
The file belongs to that chat only.

00:00:40.444 --> 00:00:45.690
It never becomes part of the knowledge of the profile, and other people never see it.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:57.545
Text, Markdown, JSON, XML, HTML, YAML and log files, spreadsheets, and PDF, Word

00:00:57.545 --> 00:01:02.440
and PowerPoint files, when those features are on.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:07.934
A document is read, split into passages, and searched by meaning.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:13.680
A very long document is refused, rather than stored where it cannot be searched.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:18.811
Charts and pictures inside a document can be described by a vision model,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.583
so that the assistant can answer about them.

00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:25.409
A figure is worth describing when it has a caption, or when the

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:26.740
text refers to it.

00:01:30.918 --> 00:01:35.626
Open Settings, Artificial Intelligence, and find the Documents section.

00:01:35.626 --> 00:01:40.273
The Index profile is the documents index that stores every attachment.

00:01:40.273 --> 00:01:43.758
Once people use it, avoid switching to another one.

00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:47.177
Document retrieval mode is the site default.

00:01:47.177 --> 00:01:50.601
Chunk gives the assistant only the matching passages.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:54.256
Hierarchical gives it the whole documents they come from.

00:01:54.722 --> 00:02:00.339
Allow document uploads in chat interactions and Allow image uploads in chat interactions

00:02:00.339 --> 00:02:04.282
turn attachments on or off for the Chat Interactions screen.

00:02:04.282 --> 00:02:06.672
Pictures need a vision deployment.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:13.509
Largest document that can be indexed is the most characters of text one document may have.

00:02:13.509 --> 00:02:15.237
Zero means no limit.

00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:21.426
Describe figures in uploaded documents decides whether charts and pictures are described.

00:02:21.426 --> 00:02:25.454
It uses a vision model and costs more, so it is the expensive

00:02:25.454 --> 00:02:26.896
part of an upload.

00:02:27.351 --> 00:02:33.318
The vision model is the Default vision deployment, in the Deployments section of the same page.

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:35.681
Without one, nothing is described.

00:02:39.891 --> 00:02:43.103
Attachments are allowed profile by profile.

00:02:43.103 --> 00:02:48.871
Open the profile, open the Knowledge tab, and tick Allow session document uploads.

00:02:49.342 --> 00:02:55.806
Describe figures in uploaded documents follows the site default, or you choose for this profile.

00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:58.722
Choose Describe figures, and click Save.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:05.007
Open a chat with the profile.

00:03:05.007 --> 00:03:09.761
An Attach files button appears, with the list of formats that it accepts.

00:03:10.212 --> 00:03:13.055
Click Attach files, and choose the file.

00:03:13.055 --> 00:03:16.022
Here it is the return policy of a company.

00:03:16.474 --> 00:03:19.546
Then ask something that only the file answers:

00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:21.614
can I return opened software?

00:03:22.085 --> 00:03:24.740
The assistant answers from the file:

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.585
no, opened software cannot be returned.

00:03:31.782 --> 00:03:32.810
Now a P.D.F.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.293
report with a chart.

00:03:34.293 --> 00:03:36.918
The sales numbers are only in the chart.

00:03:36.918 --> 00:03:41.598
The chart has a caption, Figure one, which is how the site knows it matters.

00:03:41.598 --> 00:03:43.252
Attach it the same way.

00:03:43.704 --> 00:03:44.448
Ask:

00:03:44.448 --> 00:03:47.424
which quarter sold the most units?

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:50.927
The assistant read the chart, and answers from it:

00:03:50.927 --> 00:03:52.236
the third quarter.

00:03:52.236 --> 00:03:56.597
Describing a figure takes a little longer, which is why an attachment with

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:58.505
figures is slower to prepare.

00:04:02.705 --> 00:04:04.688
A policy or a contract:

00:04:04.688 --> 00:04:09.475
ask what it says about one clause, instead of reading all of it.

00:04:10.225 --> 00:04:12.111
A report with charts:

00:04:12.111 --> 00:04:15.675
ask for the highest, the lowest or the trend.

00:04:16.425 --> 00:04:17.775
A specification:

00:04:17.775 --> 00:04:22.255
ask the assistant to compare it with another file in the same chat.

00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:29.143
Choose the documents index, allow attachments on a profile, and let people ask

00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:31.761
about their own files, charts included.

00:04:31.761 --> 00:04:33.275
Thanks for watching.

